# Security headers — applied to every route (added 2026-07-27, launch hardening).
# Lives in the publish dir (app/) so it applies no matter which netlify.toml
# Netlify treats as authoritative. Deliberately zero-breakage for this live site:
#   - Clickjacking is blocked with CSP frame-ancestors, NOT X-Frame-Options,
#     so the Counter chrome extension can still iframe voice-debate.html
#     (chrome-extension: is allowed; any external website is not).
#   - Permissions-Policy does NOT list microphone/camera/autoplay/clipboard/
#     display-capture, so voice rounds, Daily video, and the extension keep
#     their default self-access. Only clearly-unused, higher-risk features
#     are turned off.
#   - No script-src/style-src CSP yet: the pages ship many inline scripts and
#     third-party origins (Firebase, Stripe, Daily, GA, Clarity, Google Fonts,
#     CDN React), so a strict content CSP needs per-page testing before it can
#     enforce without white-screening users. Tracked as a follow-up.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), browsing-topics=(), interest-cohort=(), usb=(), serial=(), bluetooth=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' chrome-extension:;
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
